  data: {
    LLM: 'Only open with a pair of Kings or better; fold weak hands before the draw; pay attention to how many cards opponents draw.\n\nUse position: opening from late position allows you to see more passes; drawing one card can represent a strong hand (straight or flush draw) and support bluffing.\n\nTrack suit ranking for tiebreaks; in marginal spots consider whether your hand benefits from the Turkish order (e.g. flush over full house); defend openers selectively when you suspect a bluff.',
    Player: 'Only open with a pair of Kings or better; fold weak hands before the draw; pay attention to how many cards opponents draw.\n\nUse position: opening from late position allows you to see more passes; drawing one card can represent a strong hand (straight or flush draw) and support bluffing.\n\nTrack suit ranking for tiebreaks; in marginal spots consider whether your hand benefits from the Turkish order (e.g. flush over full house); defend openers selectively when you suspect a bluff.',
